'''Ward''' is a [[defence]] capable of taking damage from [[hit]]s before [[life]] or [[energy shield]]. It can only be found on item bases and uniques related to [[Expedition]] and [[Kingsmarch]].

==Mechanics==
{{See also|Receiving damage}}

Ward is not a pool that can be depleted partially; it is either unbroken or broken. 

'''Ward will break on a single hit.''' 

That is: hit damage that would reach [[energy shield]], [[life]], or [[mana]]. That hit is first taken by your Ward and breaks Ward for a duration. 

Any damage left over is taken by your energy shield, life, or mana.<ref name="Ward" />

Ward does not break in the following cases:
* when a hit is prevented (e.g. [[evasion]], [[spell dodge]])
* when a hit's damage is fully mitigated (e.g. [[immunity]], [[avoidance]], [[block]])
* when damage is fully taken from another resource first (e.g. an [[Aegis]] buff).

Broken Ward is restored after a set delay, normally 2 seconds, which is modified by {{c|mod|#% faster/slower Restoration of Ward}} modifiers. Taking hits while Ward is broken has no effect on the delay.

Ward breaking does not change the amount of Ward a character has; only the protective effect is disabled. As such, things that derive from the amount of Ward a character has, such as {{il|Nightgrip}}, remain the same even while Ward is broken.

Ward has no effect against [[damage over time]]. It does not take damage over time, nor can it be broken by it.

Ward can still break while using {{il|Dissolution of the Flesh}}: Ward breaks to take damage, necessarily before {{c|mod|Life that would be lost by taking Damage}} can be determined.

As a type of defence, Ward can be scaled by {{c|mod|% increased (Global) Defences}} from e.g. {{il|Skin of the Loyal}}, the {{Ml|BreachBodyAllDefences1}} prefix on {{il|Grasping Mail}}, or {{il|Summon Stone Golem}}.<ref name="Ward" />

Ward ''takes'' damage, it does not [[prevented damage|prevent]] damage. Accordingly, Ward does not affect the magnitude of effects based on [[damage taken]], such as [[recoup]], [[stun]], or non-damaging [[ailment]]s (e.g. {{stl|Freeze}}).<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6nDQlhecVgA</ref> It also does not lower the amount of damage counted toward {{il|Cast when Damage Taken Support}}.

